ARTICLE VI -- DURATION
========================================================================

S 6.1 This License is perpetual from the date of issuance. There is
no Change Date. No provision of this instrument converts, expires, or
opens into any other license at any future date. This is a permanent
departure from the standard 75th Avenue License, which converts its
Open Commons tier to the Mozilla Public License 2.0 after four years;
this Exclusive Edition has no Open Commons tier to convert, and none
is created by the passage of time.

S 6.2 A license granted under Article II persists for the term stated
in that license instrument. Absent a stated term, a purchased license
is perpetual for the licensee's own use, subject at all times to
Article III and to termination under S 6.4.

S 6.3 This issuance is non-transferable. It governs one named project
only. A new project requires a new issuance.

S 6.4 Termination for breach of Article III is automatic and requires
no notice. Termination of one party's rights does not affect the
rights of any other party. The license holder may additionally
terminate any individual license granted under Article II for
material breach of that license's own terms, upon the notice (if any)
stated in that license instrument.

